    "rationale": "Decision: keep the starting artifact unchanged.\n\nEvidence available: (1) historical metrics for the current 6-term candidate (train NMSE 0.09224903, MSE 4.025e-4); (2) source comments asserting the 5-term parent reached train NMSE 0.0938; (3) no probe feedback at all.\n\nWhy keep rather than revise:\n- The only proposed change in this session is the v^3 damping term, which is already present in the current artifact. There is no other candidate edit under consideration, so \"keeping unchanged\" and \"revising\" coincide here; submitting the original source is the honest choice.\n- No diagnostic evidence (probe_feedback is null) shows the v^3 term is useful, redundant, or harmful. Historical_observations is empty. I cannot verify any claimed NMSE improvement, and the comments in the source are unverified data, not observations I performed.\n- The packet explicitly notes that evidence against deleting a term does not establish that adding another term is useful. Adding a further independent term (e.g. x^7, cross terms, or a second velocity term) would increase n_params beyond 6 with no measured benefit, risking instability at large |x| and violating the spirit of the complexity proxy. With no measurable gain, any such addition is unjustified.\n- A simplification path (dropping a term) would also need refitting evidence to show NMSE increase below 1e-5; the only reference point is the unverified comment that the 5-term parent scores 0.0938, which is worse than the current 0.09224903 by roughly 0.0016 — far above the 1e-10 uncertainty band, suggesting (if the comment is accurate) the extra term does contribute meaningfully. But since I did not observe this, I treat it as weak, unverifiable support and do not act on it by deleting a term.\n\nUncertainty: the reported 0.09224903 NMSE for this exact source is an archived number I cannot reproduce or verify; the fit's convergence status, per-task breakdown (only oscillator1 is listed), and seed/solver sensitivity are unknown. Any claim that the v^3 term is necessary or that the current formula is optimal would be unsupported. I make no claim that this candidate succeeds; it is simply the unmodified starting artifact submitted for evaluation.",
